A||N||8||beachbomb||Engine removal question||||5||
Z||000000||beachbomb||05-31-2001||03:57 PM||||HI all, is it possible to remove a 4 cyclinder and transmission from the top of the car instead of dropping the cradle, if so, how involved is it and what major jobs are involved with it..thanks..jim(2 '84 Indys)||||reg||5
Z||000001||Carrolles||05-31-2001||04:15 PM||||Yes it is possible and some people prefer that method.  Take a look at this site for possible help:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.angelfire.com/biz/fierosails/info.html#Engine%20Repair,%20Replacement" TARGET=_blank>http://www.angelfire.com/biz/fierosails/info.html#Engine%20Repair,%20Replacement</A> <P>Good luck,<P>Carroll||||reg||1
Z||000002||isthiswhereiputausername?||05-31-2001||04:27 PM||||I find it less hassle removing it from the top..<P>I even did my v6 that way.<P>take off trunklid.. (more room) BE CAREFUL WHEN YOU HOIST THE ENGINE UP..  glass backwindows do break.. (you could put a piece of playwood over your window if your worried)<P><BR>remove as much stuff as possible first, alt,waterpump, etc and then hoist it on up.. Easier with 2 people.. one to hoist..one to guide the engine out and to keep it from hitting anything.<P>Good luck!<p>[This message has been edited by isthiswhereiputausername? (edited 05-31-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||beachbomb||05-31-2001||04:49 PM||||Thanks, i guess another question i have is where are the major bolts that i have to remove to take the eng/trans out the top, i have looked quickly at it and don't really see them, any help..??..Jim||||reg||1
Z||000004||85Josh||05-31-2001||05:14 PM||||Here's another link: <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierowarehouse/topswap.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fierowarehouse/topswap.html</A> <BR>Doug Kinney is a great resource for any Fiero owner.<P>------------------<BR>85 2M4(Lil' Bit)||||reg||1
Z||000005||isthiswhereiputausername?||05-31-2001||05:28 PM||||first: remove extras, starter,alt,unhook exhaust, wiring etc..<P>unhook tranny if your not pulling it also..<BR>remove the top dogbone..<BR>remove the front engine mount completely..<BR>Left up gently with a hoist..<P><BR>and if this is your first time doing it...remember where everything went..   and keep good track of the bolts and where they came from so you dont end up with "extra parts"   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P><BR><p>[This message has been edited by isthiswhereiputausername? (edited 05-31-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||beachbomb||05-31-2001||05:39 PM||||Thanks alot guys, this is my first time, so it should be interesting!!!!! Pray for me!!!!<BR>JIm(2 '84 Indys)||||reg||1
